# Unity MCP Preference

When Unity Editor work is involved, proactively use the `user-unity-mcp` tools. Do not wait for the user to ask.

Prefer MCP for:
- Console / compile errors (`Unity_ReadConsole`, `Unity_GetConsoleLogs`)
- Scene / GameObject inspection and edits (`Unity_ManageScene`, `Unity_ManageGameObject`)
- Asset find/manage (`Unity_FindProjectAssets`, `Unity_ManageAsset`)
- Script create/edit/validate when MCP fits better than raw file edits
- Menu items, editor state, camera/scene capture

Still use normal file tools for pure code reading/search when MCP isn’t needed. Prefer MCP when verifying behavior in the Editor or when file edits alone can’t confirm the result.

If Unity MCP is unavailable or auth fails, say so and fall back to file tools.
